# Content signatures of boilerplate-shaped code, one extended-regex per line.
# boilerplate-guard.sh matches new-file content against these IN ADDITION to
# the filename check, so renaming a file (orders-controller.ts -> orders-api.ts)
# does not exempt it from the scaffold mandate. Lines starting with # and blank
# lines are stripped before use.
#
# Lives next to the guard, not next to the templates, so every consumer that
# already has claude/hooks (Claude, Copilot via CLAUDE_HOOKS_HOME, Pi via
# runClaudeHook, the docker images, the flake selftest sandbox) gets it with no
# extra wiring — a guard that silently degrades to filename-only when ~/.agents
# is missing would reopen the rename hole it exists to close.
# Adding a template under agents/boilerplats/<lang>/ means adding its shape here.

# --- framework / controller shapes ---
\[ApiController\]
ControllerBase
express\.Router
Router\(\)
APIRouter\(
http\.ServeMux

# --- layered-architecture type names (whatever the file is called) ---
interface I[A-Za-z]+Repository
class [A-Za-z]+(Controller|Repository|Handler|Factory|Validator|Mapper)
type [A-Za-z]+(Controller|Repository|Handler|Factory|Validator|Mapper) struct
interface [A-Za-z]+(Command|Query|Request|Response)

# --- validator shapes ---
function validate[A-Z]
def validate_
